Z||000005||Songman||08-01-2001||12:18 PM||||80s models Trans Am and Firebird spoilers look pretty good as well, in my opinion.<P>More sleek than the original Fiero spoiler. Depends on the look you are after. They can be had for around $20 at some yards. This is not the greatest picture, but there is one on the burgundy car.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycars6.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||7
Z||000006||87FieroGTx||08-01-2001||04:14 PM|||| I like that color Songman, Nice cars!<P> I'm going to try to git one of thoes wrap-around dodge Shadow spoilers, What year/model car do they come off?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Songman||08-01-2001||07:13 PM||||I got one of the Shadow spoilers off of a 93. They made those cars for a long time. Also the Plymouth Duster is the same thing. Mine actually came off of a Duster. I was going to put it on the white coupe in the middle of the picture I showed, but I am trying to sell the car so keeping the spoiler for later use. I don't think you'll have any trouble finding one.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ronnie||08-02-2001||12:24 AM||||Hey 87Fiero, I've got one of those wraparound spoilers like Raydar pictured. It would fit real neat on an 85GT or coupe body , but is too wide for later model GT's.<BR>If you can't find one , I might just sell it!!! ||||reg||6
